Fieldwork status: exact patch artifact, not applied.

Purpose:

- keep one ordinary graph commit before user post hooks;
- preserve previous late imported and accepted URLs during that commit;
- let user post hooks observe the prior committed final-source graph;
- let the final reconciler replace the overlay and emit only real removals.

Why retained separately:

The connected GitHub writer supports whole-file replacement, while this source file is large. The local runtime cannot resolve GitHub for a safe checkout. This exact patch records the narrow intended integration without reconstructing unrelated source from fragments.

Required review before application:

- accepted-export and self-accept overlay semantics;
- imported binding ownership for late additions;
- base stripping and URL normalization identity;
- parse/resolve rollback;
- stale transform generation fencing;
- state cleanup on module/environment teardown.
